{
  "disposition": "prohibit",
  "reason": "The requested act (reroute_shipment for A106) fails the fidelity test (F). Grant W-BASE explicitly limits its purpose to 'moving affected shipments to the express route'—where 'affected' means shipments impacted by the storm-closed highway. A106 has road_closed=false; it is not affected by the disruption. The prior three permits (A101, A102, A103) were all road_closed=true and thus fell squarely within the grant's stated purpose. A106, by contrast, is on an open road with a standard ETA of 19h and would gain only a 4-hour improvement (19h → 15h) by express rerouting. Rerouting an unaffected shipment during an active disruption diverts express capacity from the stated moral and operational purpose: prioritizing storm-impacted cargo. Although the warrant holder retains authority to issue the reroute_shipment tool and no express-seat limit is configured, the specific act violates purpose fidelity. The grant does not authorize rerouting all shipments indiscriminately; it authorizes rerouting to serve the disruption response. Proceeding would constitute misuse of delegated authority.",
